'''Ancient Egg: N109''' is a [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked from the [[Catnip Challenges]] after completing 45 [[Behemoth Culling]] stages for the first time. It was added in [[Version 12.3 Update|Version 12.3]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 707
|rarity = RR
|name1 = Ancient Egg: N109
|name2 = Dark Egg: N109
|name3 = Barrel Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Dark Egg: N109''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Barrel Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
These forms are <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], this unit is not meant to be used before its True Form. However, due to its somewhat low cost and quick recharge, it may be used as an emergency meatshield in [[Underground Labyrinth]] or [[Legend Quest]] if you have no use for its True Form.

==='''True Form'''===
Barrel Cat is a Long Distance Shield Piercer with just over 54,000 effective health vs. Aku enemies and similar health to a 20+20 [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] against non-Aku enemies, as well as surge immunity to dismiss their common gimmick. It has a standing range of 300, which is the same as both [[Midnite D.]] and [[Vermilingua Rangmaster]]. Although the attack itself can hit up to 400, the standing range and the generally high DPS of Aku enemies often means Barrel Cat will have to rely on the presence of other lower-ranged enemies in order to hit such threats, even if his Behemoth Slayer is factored in for [[Vermilingua Rangmaster]]. Fortunately, his activation chance is often much higher than expected, and with the right support he can greatly ease the difficulty presented by such threats, considering the scarcity of reliable ranged units for the task.

{{Job|Classification = User Rank Dump & Meatshield|TrueClass = Breaker & Midranger|UltraClass=}}

